README.md-51-Requirements are organized into four BMW vehicle domains: **Interior & Comfort**, **Exterior & Utility**, **Digital Experience & Controls**, and **Driving & Powertrain**. This keeps the review surface coherent while still ranking no more than ten requirements inside each domain.
README.md-52-
README.md:53:Within those four stable navigation domains, PM derives evidence-based outcome clusters such as seating comfort, cargo access, connected access, parking confidence, and ride and handling. PMs can rename, split, merge, reorder, and move requirements without losing their citations.
README.md-54-
README.md-55-## Grounding and provenance
README.md-56-
README.md:57:`scripts/ingest-evidence.ps1` reads the supplied ZIP. It creates `data/evidence.json` with exact filename, sheet, source row, original feedback ID, vehicle, market, classification, and original text. It also creates `data/context.json`, containing 1,003 customer-study rows, 12 sales-volume rows, source-file metadata, and verified PDF page counts. All eight original files are extracted to `data/sources/` for direct inspection. The current generated feedback store contains 13,771 classification rows.
README.md-58-
README.md-59-Frequency is calculated from unique feedback IDs within a feature, not spreadsheet rows. This prevents one comment assigned to several classifications from being presented as several customers. Low-quality and unclassified feedback remains in the evidence store but is excluded from requirements.
README.md-60-
README.md:61:Requirement language, feature grouping, ownership routing, and time-to-market fit are generated by deterministic, inspectable prototype logic. The application remains demonstrable without an API key. OpenAI-assisted email redrafting, stakeholder-response interpretation, and live cited market research are disabled until the server key is configured.
README.md-62-
README.md-63-## Current prototype boundaries
README.md-64-
README.md:65:- Feedback, customer-study, sales-volume, and original option-list files are ingested. Ranked claims attach matching feedback, study, and vehicle/market sales records with workbook-row citations.
README.md-66-- Original PDFs and verified page counts are available, but PDF text extraction is intentionally omitted because no reliable parser is installed. No PDF content or page citation is fabricated.
README.md:67:- Requirement grouping and planning estimates remain deterministic demo logic. Stakeholder-response interpretation and email drafting use the OpenAI Responses API; external market research uses its web-search tool, rejects reports without URL citations, and admits only requirement candidates that retain a URL returned by the search.
README.md-68-- Decision events are written to an append-only server NDJSON log and mirrored in browser storage; a production deployment should add authentication, signatures, backups, and formal retention controls.
README.md-69-- Two records explicitly labeled **Team-authored demo history** seed the memory experience. They are never presented as verified BMW decisions. New application events are labeled genuine application events.
README.md-70-- Email is drafted only. The application does not send external messages.
